From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:06:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 87/87] web-app: say a fresh failed download may still be
 arriving
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Core gives a post-message that no relay has yet ten minutes before failing
it, because its sender may still be uploading a large attachment (core/0034).
Slower uploads can take longer, so a bare "download failed" on a message
that arrived minutes ago reads like the attachment is lost when it most
likely is not.

A failed download on a message received less than an hour ago now reads
"May still be arriving — try again in a few minutes" instead. One
`DownloadFailedLabel` component replaces the four "download failed" spans in
the download placeholder and the one in Message.tsx's plain fallback. The
string is fork-only and goes into _untranslated_en.json.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
